bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_glyph_run_over_512_device_px_not_painted_2026-11-28, 0, "A text run whose device font size is above about 512 px is painted wrong. Chrome 159: <button style=font-size:200px;padding:4px>Go</button> label ink spans device columns 60..1053 at k=4 (800 device px font) and 15..262 at k=1; Simple paints 21..649 at k=4, about 512/800 of the size. A <span style=font-size:800px;line-height:1>Go</span> at k=1 (window 1200x900) paints NO ink in Simple (Chrome 40..1033 on row 895 band). Layout width is right (box borders match after the measure-cap fix); the glyph raster / glyph-cache path caps or drops sizes above 512 device px. Not located."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_glyph_run_over_512_device_px_not_painted_2026-11-28, P3, open, "web render: glyph runs above ~512 device px font size paint shrunken (k=4) or not at all (800 px at k=1)", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/text_layout/font_renderer.spl, 1, "<button style=font-size:200px>Go</button> at device scale 4, or <span style=font-size:800px>Go</span> at scale 1; compare label ink columns with Chrome 159", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_glyph_run_over_512_device_px_not_painted_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 button-label-cluster lane: found while pinning web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28 (its spec does not assert the label ink for this reason). Candidates to read first: font_renderer.spl FONT_LCD_MAX_SIZE_PX / 'font_size <= 512' gate (~1790) and the 512 reference cap (~1947); the paint path for a run whose size exceeds those."

